WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.939
Speaker 1: I got a really great email from
a viewer named Wade who said covid has taken

00:00:04.939 --> 00:00:06.650
away our ability to behave.

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.440
And I think it goes much further.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:14.280
There seems to be almost like a covid induced
psychosis that is plaguing this country and

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:15.340
some other parts of the world.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:16.850
And I want to go through it today.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:22.060
I already discussed on yesterday's bonus show
that a number of unruly passengers on airplanes

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.080
are being reported to the FAA.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:28.080
That number is increasing dramatically and
much of it is related to where it's triggered

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.300
by mask's people angry about someone else
wearing a mask.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:36.690
People angry about someone else not wearing
a mask, masks and just getting back to being

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:40.620
in close quarters with people on airplanes
is causing many unruly passengers.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.289
We talked about that yesterday, but as Wade
wrote to me, he said, quote, As more and more

00:00:45.289 --> 00:00:49.410
people attend events and begin to travel,
there's an increasing level of violence and

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:54.229
frustration that on the surface might seem
to result of not having to practice decorum

00:00:54.229 --> 00:00:58.960
and civility in similar situations for the
past year due to the pandemic.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:02.460
I think there's something to this one category.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:06.420
Fan behavior at sporting events in Washington,
D.C.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:12.689
Fans fan runs onto court during Washington
Wizards Game four in latest act of misbehavior,

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:14.750
games just started and there is a rash of
this.

00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:21.390
The seventy Sixers, Knicks and Jazz have had
to ban fans following playoff game incidents

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.060
involving players.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:24.060
Then it grew more.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:30.780
And now five NBA venues have banned fans for
disrespectful behavior during games.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.390
And it's not just happening in basketball
and it's not just happening in the U.S..

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:41.680
In Glasgow, Scotland, fans of the Rangers
football club went nuts, thousands of them

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:47.880
defying covid warnings against large gatherings,
getting together in George Square to celebrate

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:53.420
the Rangers winning their first Scottish Premiership
championship in 10 years.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:59.689
The square was just strewn with broken bottles
and bags, and there were flares launched and

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:01.270
all sorts of stuff.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.270
Riot police came out.

00:02:03.270 --> 00:02:12.780
And then lastly, on the sports front, Marcellus
Razorbacks fans in Arkansas led to a bunch

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.170
of arrests and charges.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:19.580
One such fan pleaded guilty to violating the
face coverings rule.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.760
Then we have all of the airline stuff.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.670
A report from CNBC explaining that a flight
attendant union chief says unruly behavior

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.470
from plane passengers has never been this
bad.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:33.980
We mentioned yesterday that a Southwest Airlines
passenger punched out a flight attendant's

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:36.610
teeth last week, I believe two teeth.

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:41.879
It's actually so bad that American Airlines
is extending their suspension of alcohol service

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:44.830
because they believe the alcohol can be an
aggravating factor.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.409
Yeah, it can.

00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:48.610
And then the road rage has just exploded.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:53.650
Some examples include a rash of road rage
incident in North Carolina, in Los Angeles

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.800
and Colorado, in Atlanta.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:01.020
I don't believe this is as simple as people
have gotten used to not having to behave because

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:05.209
they've been home for a year plus and now
they're around people and they forgot how

00:03:05.209 --> 00:03:06.209
to behave.

00:03:06.209 --> 00:03:08.849
That just doesn't strike me as the explanation.

00:03:08.849 --> 00:03:13.060
Some of this is that there are people who
just no longer care about decorum.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.700
Some are furious about the pandemic and about
shutdowns.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.080
And instead of just being glad to be back
to doing things, they're going nuts and they're

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.580
taking their fury out on others.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:27.560
For other people, there is just the difficulty
of reintegrating after being as many people

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.659
were and continue to be so scared to do anything.

00:03:31.659 --> 00:03:33.890
And there's a sort of PTSD taking place.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:38.210
It's coming out in some weird ways for other
people.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:45.000
I think the becoming unaccustomed to being
in groups has created a sort of agoraphobia

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.380
and some people stay home as a result of it.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:51.790
Others just kind of feel stressed when they
go out.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.560
And then you have people who are reacting
by lashing out in some of these weird ways.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:57.930
I think this is going to continue for some
time.

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:01.989
We've not even we're only starting to see
the resumption in travel we're seeing.

00:04:01.989 --> 00:04:05.799
Oh, but let me mention one other thing.

00:04:05.799 --> 00:04:08.470
Commuting is horrible psychologically.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:12.340
People who have long commutes, it's just a
real drag on quality of life.

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:18.650
We know this from study after study, not having
to commute for so long for many people and

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:23.260
then being dropped back into a commute as
traffic is starting to build again.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:26.550
I can only imagine that that's having a real
impact on a lot of people's.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:33.620
Psychological state, it took months to adjust
to what was a new reality during the pandemic.

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:39.169
I think it's going to take at least a few
months to adjust to getting out of it, if

00:04:39.169 --> 00:04:43.120
indeed we continue to get out of it and hopefully
we will as vaccination continue.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.490
But I don't think that there's any easy solution
to this.

00:04:46.490 --> 00:04:51.320
Let me know what you think and we'll have
more on this on our Instagram, where you can

00:04:51.320 --> 00:05:43.830
find us at 

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:56.090
The 
David Pakman Show.

